---
/* Cell grid: cells (<Card>s or anything with an ink rule) collapse into one
 * ruled table - no gap, every cell pulled 1px up and left over its
 * neighbour so two cells share one rule, the grid padded 1px back so the
 * outer frame stays inside it.
 *   columns  a fixed count on wide screens, one column at 880px and below;
 *            with two columns an odd last cell spans the row
 *   min      without `columns`: as many columns as fit cells of this width
 *            (wrapped in min(100%, ...), so a narrow screen never scrolls)
 * `tag` picks the element (a list of cells is a ul / ol). */
interface Props {
  class?: string;
  columns?: number;
  min?: string;
  tag?: "div" | "ul" | "ol";
}

const { columns, min = "280px", tag = "div", class: extraClass } = Astro.props;
const Tag = tag;
const template = columns
  ? `repeat(${columns}, minmax(0, 1fr))`
  : `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, ${min}), 1fr))`;
---

<Tag
  style={`--mb-cell-columns: ${template}`}
  class:list={[
    "mb-cell-grid",
    { "mb-cell-grid-fixed": columns, "mb-cell-grid-pair": columns === 2 },
    extraClass,
  ]}
>
  <slot />
</Tag>

<style>
  .mb-cell-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--mb-cell-columns);
    gap: 0;
    padding: 1px 0 0 1px;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .mb-cell-grid > :global(*) {
    margin: -1px 0 0 -1px;
  }

  .mb-cell-grid-pair > :global(:last-child:nth-child(odd)) {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .mb-cell-grid-fixed {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
